af4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6162fbab6ed13040ec851a36"], "question": {"text": "The correct order of stability of following carbocations is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FRXGcNYy2D7bI4DGjt78FgNdp-SUxjyWkd3dUgvD8fTA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "0ff57b", "text": "$\\mathrm{C}\\gt\\mathrm{B}\\gt\\mathrm{A}\\gt\\mathrm{D}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928a9fe"}, {"id": "014173", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}\\gt\\mathrm{B}\\gt\\mathrm{C}\\gt\\mathrm{D}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928a9ff"}, {"id": "0e2d8d", "text": "$\\mathrm{B}\\gt\\mathrm{C}\\gt\\mathrm{A}\\gt\\mathrm{D}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa00"}, {"id": "906210", "text": "$\\mathrm{C}\\gt\\mathrm{A}\\gt\\mathrm{B}\\gt\\mathrm{D}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa01"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa02", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["6162fbaf6ed13040ec851d20"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following statements are correct?\nA. Glycerol is purified by vacuum distillation because it decomposes at its normal boiling point.\nB. Aniline can be purified by steam distillation as aniline is miscible in water.\nC. Ethanol can be separated from ethanol water mixture by azeotropic distillation because it forms azeotrope.\nD. An organic compound is pure, if mixed M.P. is remained same.\nChoose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "5f67fb", "text": "A, B, C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa03"}, {"id": "711ad8", "text": "A, C, D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa04"}, {"id": "130f93", "text": "A, B, D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa05"}, {"id": "12f39b", "t