</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa1c"}, {"id": "085c9d", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F00acac01-6b66-48c8-be81-4dc40b48eda3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 131px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa1d"}, {"id": "f7c02d", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe458fad7-ab24-49f0-aa84-844d3dd51657-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 121px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa1e"}, {"id": "62fe24", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1d52a8c8-0258-460b-8f1d-b17c7225c755-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa1f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa20", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["617aa9f6ef3fe65ad8e8442d"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following compound (X)<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7Pid5N_5hHHURk_YzGI4pW-l13z7UrIhnpoHjXqxED4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br />The most stable and least stable carbon radicals, respectively, produced by homolytic cleavage of corresponding \\(\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}\\) bond are :"}, "options": [{"id": "f48b84", "text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa21"}, {"id": "a78e07", "text": "III, II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa22"}, {"id": "9e778a", "text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa23"}, {"id": "98fe7f", "text": "II, I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa24"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa25", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e69"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List I with List II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\"> <tbody> <tr> <td> </td> <td>LIST I (Technique)</td> <td> </td> <td>LIST II (Application)</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A.</td> <td>Distillation</td> <td>I.</td> <td>Separation of glycerol from spent-lye</td> </tr> <tr> <td>B.</td> <td>Fractional distillation</td> <td>II.</td> <td>Aniline - Water mixture</td> </tr> <tr> <td>C.</td> <td>Steam distillation</td> <td>III.</td> <td>Separation of crude oil fractions</td> </tr> <tr> <td>D.</td> <td>Distillation under reduced pressure</td> <td>IV.</td> <td>Chloroform-Aniline</td> </tr> </tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ff1e63", "text": "A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa26"}, {"id": "4c400c", "text": "A-IV, B-III, C-II. D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa27"}, {"id": "d06e94", "text": "A-I. B-II, C-IV, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa28"}, {"id": "7de1e1", "text": "A-II, B-III. C-I, D-IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa29"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b25"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following is an aromatic compound?"}, "options": [{"id": "6c4194", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8a8f4784-d223-428c-8264-6974ede6a9aa-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 115px; height: 106px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2b"}, {"id": "ad3dd8", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F08a6942c-b854-4eef-9270-41ab72af30fa-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 86px; height: 96px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2c"}, {"id": "225c3e", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F329b4146-16df-48b5-a953-36862b4f201c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 115px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2d"}, {"id": "7301e1", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb4c355ea-7b04-4577-a1ab-81aaecfe5533-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 122px; height: 87px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa2f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6162fbab6ed13040ec851a2e"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:<br />Statement I : Hyperconjugation is not a permanent effect.<br />Statement II : In general, greater the number of alkyl groups attached to a positively charged C -atom, greater is the hyperconjugation interaction and stabilization of the cation.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below"}, "options": [{"id": "9f0e3d", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa30"}, {"id": "de28c0", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa31"}, {"id": "19ac17", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa32"}, {"id": "756817", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa33"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa34", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["6162fbaf6ed13040ec851d20"], "question": {"text": "<p>The fragrance of flowers is due to the presence of some steam volatile organic compounds called essential oils. These are generally insoluble in water at room temperature but are miscible with water vapour in the vapour phase. A suitable method for the extraction of these oils from the flowers is:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9632b1", "text": "crystallisation", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa35"}, {"id": "b1ce6d", "text": "distillation under reduced pressure", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa36"}, {"id": "fa2b5f", "text": "distillation", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa37"}, {"id": "4fe538", "text": "steam distillation", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa38"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa39", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b25"], "question": {"text": "<p>Among the following, the aromatic compounds are :</p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F57b73af2-a95e-4219-b046-7cfae0578dfe-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 159px;\" /></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt\">Choose the correct answer from the following options :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e5f543", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3a"}, {"id": "8a5473", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3b"}, {"id": "de69fe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3c"}, {"id": "9b1761", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5654"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Statement</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math> Aniline is less basic than acetamide.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Statement</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math> In aniline, the lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom is delocalised over benzene ring due to resonance and hence less available to a proton.<br />Choose the most appropriate option ;"}, "options": [{"id": "ad9610", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa3f"}, {"id": "9b4986", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa40"}, {"id": "9172ea", "text": "Both statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa41"}, {"id": "b270c4", "text": "Both statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa42"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa43", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["630cf468cc7f05dc29507ea0"], "question": {"text": "<p>Chromatographic technique/s based on the principle of differential adsorption is/are<br/>A. Column chromatography B. Thin layer chromatography C. Paper chromatography</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fceb4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa44"}, {"id": "fa1a0c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa45"}, {"id": "915f51", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa46"}, {"id": "71cee4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa47"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa48", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["6162fbac6ed13040ec851b25"], "question": {"text": "Correct order of stability of carbanion is -\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FYGYeze4gMdOA_aKjqQWW8aAIOFH3ZcoR3n2ihzzkttQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "1fd4dc", "text": "\\(d > a > c > b\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa49"}, {"id": "a0aa3d", "text": "a \\( > \\) b \\( > \\) c \\( > \\) d", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4a"}, {"id": "0b37ec", "text": "\\(d > c > b > a\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4b"}, {"id": "f5042c", "text": "\\(c > b > d > \\) a", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87db"], "question": {"text": "<p>Compound(s) which will liberate carbon dioxide with sodium bicarbonate solution is/are :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0f06f3d4-441d-40e9-88b5-a5f6805c1220-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 480px; height: 128px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "91e962", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4e"}, {"id": "7e11fa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa4f"}, {"id": "dd9034", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa50"}, {"id": "b7b857", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa51"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa52", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6162fbab6ed13040ec851a34"], "question": {"text": "The set of meta directing functional groups from the following sets is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0abea8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>NHR</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa53"}, {"id": "90e163", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COOR</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa54"}, {"id": "cb12cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>CHO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COR</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa55"}, {"id": "2ca3da", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>CHO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NHCOCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>COOR</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa56"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa57", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ac7"], "question": {"text": "The functional group that shows negative resonance effect is:"}, "options": [{"id": "7af22e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa58"}, {"id": "92c925", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa59"}, {"id": "6a17f6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5a"}, {"id": "230438", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OR</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6162fbab6ed13040ec851a2e"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I : Hyperconjugation is a permanent effect.</p><p>Statement II : Hyperconjugation in ethyl cation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> involves the overlapping of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></math> bond with empty <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> orbital of other carbon.</p><p>Choose the correct option:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4374cf", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5d"}, {"id": "f56ad6", "text": "Statement I&nbsp;is incorrect but statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5e"}, {"id": "66bda2", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa5f"}, {"id": "f7dedd", "text": "Both Statement I and statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa60"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa61", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5676"], "concepts": ["6162fbab6ed13040ec851a36"], "question": {"text": "<p>The ascending acidity order of the following H atoms is </p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb0d39b46-0b97-4d44-8d57-67f6eb29439a.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 160px;\"/></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4bc84b", "text": "C &lt; D &lt; B &lt; A ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa62"}, {"id": "1ccd88", "text": " A &lt; B &lt; C &lt; D ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa63"}, {"id": "e77281", "text": "A &lt; B &lt; D &lt; C ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa64"}, {"id": "348572", "text": "D &lt; C &lt; B &lt; A ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f782ee0e063d928aa65"}], "questionLabels": []}